Property:
	Tag: [Guide, Module]
	Module: Chemistry

The **Chemistry** module draws molecules, reactions, and mechanisms with electron-pushing arrows. Hover a drawing and click *Edit drawing* (or *Edit board*) to change it in the drawing tool, like ChemDraw. Back to [[Welcome]]; equations are in [[Math]].

## One structure

Chem: -30 (<90 O) -330 -30

A Chem block holds one structure, here 2-butanol. You draw it; the note keeps it as one short line of bonds with their direction in degrees (`-30` goes up-right, `-330` down-right), branches in parentheses (`<90 O`: a wedge up to an O), and atoms. Bare corners are carbons, and hydrogens are added by themselves.

## A mechanism on a board

Board:
	Chem {X: 14.7, Y: 37.8}: O@o^-:3
	Chem {X: 76.4, Y: 0}: H >35 C@c (-0@cb Br@br) (-100 H) <:250 H
	Chem {X: 65.6, Y: 157.4}: O -0[Dashed] C@ts (-0[Dashed] Br) (-90 H) (<235 H) <:305 H
	Chem {X: 243.4, Y: 155.4}: O -0 C (-80 H) (<:290 H) <325 H

	{Chem: +} {X: 353.1, Y: 194}

	Chem {X: 368.7, Y: 193.7}: Br^-
	Arrow {X: 8.8, Y: 206, Length: 51.2}:
		slow {Side: Below}
	Arrow {X: 186.6, Y: 206, Length: 51.2}:
	Arrow {From: o.lp, To: c}:
	Arrow {From: cb, To: br, Curve: 70}:

	backside attack, **inversion** of configuration {X: 5.6, Y: 100.3, Size: 0.85em, TextAlign: Center, Width: 227.2}

	transition state {X: 74.1, Y: 253.7, Size: 0.85em, TextAlign: Center, Color: Accent}

- A **Board** places each block where its X and Y say. Alt + drag a block on it right here, or open *Edit board* and drag anything: click a bond to pick up a whole structure, or drag a box around a chunk. Click empty space to let go.
- `O@o^-:3` is an oxygen named `o`, charged −1, with three lone pairs. `Arrow {From: o.lp, To: c}` starts at the lone pair facing the carbon named `c`; `cb` names the C–Br bond.
- The text is ordinary text blocks: double-click one in *Edit board* to change it. Text inside an arrow sits above or below it.
- Text on an arrow slides along it or to its other side when you drag it, and leaves the arrow when you drop it farther away; drop text on an arrow to put it there.
- The Color button opens the Palette: the theme's colors, a palette (Element has the usual element colors; import your own), the colors you used lately, and any hex code. Pick one, then click what to color.
- A Board with no Chem blocks opens with just arrows, text, and color: chemistry tools show where there is chemistry.
- Keys pick tools: V select, E erase, 1 2 3 bonds, W wedge, R benzene, D lone pair, A curved arrow, T text, G color (hover a tool for its key). On an atom or a bond, element letters and 1 2 3 change it instead. Setting → Hotkey changes them (search "Drawing").
- In *Edit board*, a right click undoes what the tool does (the lone pair tool takes a pair away) or opens a menu (an arrow's kind, head, and color); a right drag moves around. Hold a tool button for more tools of its kind. On a touch screen, hold your finger instead of right-clicking.

