	Chem {X: 0, Y: 4}: &1 =30 -330 =270 -210 =150 -&1
	Chem {X: 145.1, Y: 0}: &1 =30 -330 * (-30 Br) =270 -210 =150 -&1

	{Chem: +} {X: 271.8, Y: 36}

	Chem {X: 287.3, Y: 35.7}: Br
	Arrow {X: 83.3, Y: 48, Length: 56.2}:
		{Chem: Br_2} {Side: Above}

		{Chem: FeBr_3} {Side: Below}

## From LaTeX

Chem:
	\schemestart \chemfig{*6(=-=-=-)} \arrow{->[Br_2][FeBr_3]} \chemfig{*6(=-=(-Br)-=-)} \+ HBr \schemestop

chemfig pasted from a LaTeX note draws as it is. *Edit drawing* turns it into a Board like the one above, with every structure, arrow, and label pinned where it is.

## In a sentence

The combustion of methane: {Chem: CH_4 + 2O_2 -> CO_2 + 2H_2O}.

Bond length and label spacing are in Setting → Module → Chemistry.
